  L-profile doubler valleys (analytic): near k_i = pi, s = sin k on |k|>=b2, so eps^2 = m^2 + sum sin^2(delta_i) + (box axes) k^2;
  A_ii = cos(2 delta_i) - 1 = -2 sin^2 delta_i; for T << 1/a each of the 7 valleys has the box partition function up to O((Ta)^2): f_edge -> 7/8.

